'''Dagshund''' (だっふんど, ''Daffundo'') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]]. He was added in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Dagshund
|image = E 041.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Hyaluronan Mountain|Sub-chapter 3 - Hyaluronan Mountain]]<br>
'''CotC''': [[Earth (Cats of the Cosmos)|Chapter 1 - Earth]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Hole Lotta Somethin'|Sub-chapter 5 - Hole Lotta Somethin']]
|money drop = 700¢ - 2,765¢
}}

==Enemy==
Dagshund has slow movement speed but attacks quickly with high area damage; yet his slow animation and low range balances this out. He isn't intimidating alone, but he is usually spawned in groups or rapidly when included in a stage, and his very high health, combined with his singular knockback, can make him very difficult to take down. In later stages, his strength magnification can exceed 1000%, giving him more than 600,000 HP to absorb fire while his 30,000 damage decimates whatever he touches.

==Strategy==
Dagshund, despite his sheer offense, is somewhat easy to stall consistently. Smaller meatshields ([[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]], etc...) generally fare better than tanks for impeding him while backliners like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] take him out. Stacking [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cats]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cats]] can also work if you have enough meatshields to stall the Dagshund.

As Dagshund has no Immunities, [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless Cats]] like [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]], [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]] and [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] can provide assistance with their Knockback abilities. He can also be "stepping stone" for [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Cats with Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Waves]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surges]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosions]] to hit whatever that's behind him.

